      "body": "Gradient finalization currently skips SP-marked parameters when the root model has `sequence_parallel=False`. A composite model can enable SP in its vision transformer while leaving language SP off, so those vision LayerNorm gradients must still be summed across TP ranks.\n\nUse each parameter's `sequence_parallel` marker independently of the root flag. Keep average-gradient precedence, QK-normalization handling, frozen/unused parameters, and TP1 behavior unchanged. Related to NVIDIA-NeMo/Megatron-Bridge#6662.\n\nValidation:\n- Two H100 ranks: `TestAllReduceLNGrads` — 9 passed, 1 expected skip (root SP with TP1). New cases cover independent module SP, rank-distinct gradients, and unmarked/frozen/unused parameters; existing normalization and embedding checks also pass.\n- Black, isort, Ruff, and pylint pass on both changed files. The `autoformat.sh` wrapper requires Git >=2.31; this workstation has 2.25.1, so its component tools were run directly. Optional mypy reports missing local PyTorch/pytest dependencies and existing typing findings outside this change.\n- Fresh independent review completed with no blocking findings. Signed commit and DCO included.\n\nNo external code was copied.",
